 "segments": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 3.08,
   "t": "ordered lethal drugs, then hit cancel one second later."
  },
  {
   "s": 3.88,
   "e": 6.64,
   "t": "By the early 2000s, hospitals nationwide"
  },
  {
   "s": 6.64,
   "e": 9.2,
   "t": "began adopting automated dispensing cabinets"
  },
  {
   "s": 9.2,
   "e": 11.2,
   "t": "known as PIXIS med station systems"
  },
  {
   "s": 11.2,
   "e": 12.88,
   "t": "to regulate pharmaceuticals."
  },
  {
   "s": 13.82,
   "e": 15.98,
   "t": "However, Charles Cullen quickly discovered"
  },
  {
   "s": 15.98,
   "e": 17.62,
   "t": "a critical software vulnerability"
  },
  {
   "s": 17.62,
   "e": 19.2,
   "t": "within the terminal's architecture."
  },
  {
   "s": 20.14,
   "e": 22.86,
   "t": "He would enter requests for dangerous medications"
  },
  {
   "s": 22.86,
   "e": 25.6,
   "t": "like de joxin, insulin, or norepinephrine."
  },
  {
   "s": 25.78,
   "e": 27.6,
   "t": "But the moment the physical drawer released,"
  },
  {
   "s": 27.6,
   "e": 29.1,
   "t": "he pressed the cancel button."
  },
  {
   "s": 30.1,
   "e": 32.26,
   "t": "The terminal logged the transaction as canceled"
  },
  {
   "s": 32.26,
   "e": 33.76,
   "t": "and avoided billing the patient,"
  },
  {
   "s": 33.96,
   "e": 36.24,
   "t": "yet the lethal vial was already concealed"
  },
  {
   "s": 36.24,
   "e": 37.54,
   "t": "inside Cullen's pocket."
  },
  {
   "s": 38.52,
   "e": 40.28,
   "t": "At Somerset Medical Center,"
  },
  {
   "s": 40.6,
   "e": 42.9,
   "t": "his behavioral inhibition collapsed entirely,"
  },
  {
   "s": 43.28,
   "e": 45.94,
   "t": "leading him to target young, recovering patients"
  },
  {
   "s": 45.94,
   "e": 47.08,
   "t": "slated for discharge."
  },
  {
   "s": 47.98,
   "e": 50.68,
   "t": "In contrast, his psychological signature,"
  },
  {
   "s": 51.12,
   "e": 53.04,
   "t": "the unchanging emotional gratification"
  },
  {
   "s": 53.04,
   "e": 56.18,
   "t": "compelling his crimes, was his profound God complex."
  },
  {
   "s": 56.18,
   "e": 62.38,
   "t": "He experienced a fleeting sense of omnipotence, imagining himself elevated above medicine and"
  },
  {
   "s": 62.38,
   "e": 64.84,
   "t": "destiny as the sole arbiter of who survived."
  },
  {
   "s": 65.48,
   "e": 67.44,
   "t": "Episode 4 of Amber Eyes."
  },
  {
   "s": 67.78,
   "e": 69.82,
   "t": "Watch the full documentary via the bio-link."
  }
 ]
}